Subject: [PATCH] PHPUnit 9: run WordPress-style hyphenated test files by path

PHPUnit 9's StandardTestSuiteLoader derives the expected class name from the
test file's basename and, when matching it against the declared classes, only
bridges the "\" and "_" separators. WordPress/PMC name test files with hyphens
(e.g. test-class-foo.php) but name the classes with underscores (Test_Class_Foo),
so `phpunit tests/test-class-foo.php` fails with "Class ... could not be found".

Normalising hyphens to underscores in the derived name lets a single test file
be run by its path. A PHP class name can never contain a hyphen, so this is
safe and is a no-op for files whose names already match their class.

Target: /usr/share/php/phpunit/vendor/phpunit/phpunit/src/Runner/StandardTestSuiteLoader.php
--- a/src/Runner/StandardTestSuiteLoader.php
+++ b/src/Runner/StandardTestSuiteLoader.php
@@ -36,4 +36,4 @@ final class StandardTestSuiteLoader implements TestSuiteLoader
     public function load(string $suiteClassFile): ReflectionClass
     {
-        $suiteClassName = basename($suiteClassFile, '.php');
+        $suiteClassName = str_replace('-', '_', basename($suiteClassFile, '.php'));
         $loadedClasses  = get_declared_classes();
